{
  "summary": "Restricts libbitcoinkernel to allow only one active logging connection per process at a time. Renames the entry point to btck_global_logging_connection_create, fails subsequent concurrent connection attempts, and replaces the global btck_logging_set_min_level with a handle-specific btck_logging_connection_set_min_level defaulting to Info on creation.",
  "problem": "The underlying KernelLogger is a process-wide singleton, so all connections share the same log stream and minimum log level. Exposing an API that allowed creating multiple btck_LoggingConnection handles gave consumers the false impression that independent loggers could be instantiated.",
  "evidence": [
   "Description notes: 'Kernel logging is inherently global: KernelLogger is a process-wide singleton, so every connection receives every log entry and shares the minimum level. Multiple btck_LoggingConnection handles give the false impression of independent loggers.'"
  ],
